            "review_title": "Review at Ruby Soho Saigon",
            "review_text": "Traveler of the Wild\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam66 contributions\n1\nAmazing location, decor and friendly service. Very very limited food and drink selection\nNov 2018 • Friends\nRuby Soho is an extremely well-appointed bar on one of the main roads (Pham Van Nghi) in the Phu My Hung international neighbourhood in suburban district 7 of Saigon. The bar itself is packed full of movie, tv and comic memorabilia and collectables from many genres. It's worth a visit just for the decor. It's also spacious with several seating options and a large bar to sit at (rectangular shaped bar). Ruby Soho also stays open late most nights and the service is quick and friendly. However, the big downside is that the drinks/food selection is very very limited. They offer only the most basic industrial beer/cider brands on draft but no real sign of craft beers/ciders and an extremely limited food menu. Definitely worth a quick visit if you fancy a look at the decor and a quick beer at the end of the night.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten December 18, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
