            "review_title": "Review at Ruby Soho Saigon",
            "review_text": "Steve K\nToronto, Canada23 contributions\n1\nGood (Atmosphere & Drinks)...Bad (Food Price & Quality)\nNov 2018 • Couples\nThis place has a good vibe with a retro funky atmosphere as well as fine range of music...however, its Achilles heel is that you can really only go there for drinks because the price of the food is too high and the quality of it is just too low. For one of many examples, small nachos are 180,000 vnd and the nacho chips are just dorito chips (like the snack) whereas La Fiesta and Lost Boys (both in D7 too) provide the real deal nachos of much higher quality with more reasonable price! This type of situation is a common theme throughout the food menu - skimping on the quality, excessive on the price. Overall, a good place to go for drinks, but eat before or after your visit.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 13, 2018",
